From 96038469ce6e4a42470a68ff9d0809946438dc16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker placement: a refused pool repin no longer
 suppresses the origin repin

Review t_01a1d5dba1ad82b9 of PR #2362 (t_01a1d560c6d3bc3c), follow-up card t_01a1d5edeefa8430.

`kanban_worker_placement` kept one `_selfcheck_refused` entry per card for Board refusals of the stranded-card
self-check pool repin, and `_repin_target` passed that same entry to
`kanban_worker_pickup_gate.origin_target` as `refused_at`. A gate-refused enrolled ready card whose pool repin the
Board refused was then never asked to go home (`--runs-on machine:<origin>`) at that revision: no reserve, one
capability_mismatch comment, stranded until its revision moved.

Fix: origin-repin refusals get their own map, `_origin_refused`. `_repin_target` returns which map a Board refusal
of the repin it chose is recorded in (`_remember_refusal(refusals, ...)`), so a refused pool repin still lets the
origin repin be asked once at that revision, and a refused origin repin still suppresses only origin retries at
that revision. The persistent/transient status rule is unchanged.

Five whys:
1. Why did the card stay stranded? origin_target returned "nothing to ask" at its revision.
2. Why? refused_at matched the revision.
3. Why? refused_at was the pool self-check's refusal, not an origin refusal.
4. Why? both repins shared one per-card refusal map.
5. Why? the origin repin (PR #2362) reused the self-check's map instead of keying its own.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_worker_origin_repin_refusal.py (stranded card whose wire row has a
malformed `requires`, so the self-check targets the pool and every pickup gate refuses it).
RED on main: "the origin repin was never asked at revision 4" (repins after the refused pool repin: []), and the
refused-origin case asks [pool] only. GREEN: the second tick repins to machine:hub at revision 4, no reserves,
exactly one capability_mismatch event and gate comment; a refused origin repin is not re-asked at that revision
(4 ticks: [pool, origin]) and a new revision asks pool then origin once more.
